1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Fast cars. Fast girls. Fast living.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Roadracers is a action, crime, drama film directed by Robert Rodriguez.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
In the 1950s, guitar-playing drifter Dude Delaney wanders into a quiet town looking to play music and
generally cause trouble, much to the chagrin of the local sheriff, known as Sarge.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
While palling around with his B-movie-obsessed friend Nixer, Dude meets the beautiful Donna, and is offered a
position in a rockabilly band, but the sheriff is intent on getting rid of him by any means necessary.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Dude Delaney, played by David Arquette.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Donna, played by Salma Hayek Pinault.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Nixer, played by John Hawkes.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Teddy Leather, played by Jason Wiles.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
J.T., played by O'Neal Compton.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Miles, played by Kevin McCarthy.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Roadracers is a 1994 made-for-television film directed by Robert Rodriguez, his
second feature film following the success of his 1992 debut, El Mariachi.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
The film originally aired on Showtime Network as part of their Rebel Highway series that took the titles of 1950s-era B-movies and applied them to original films starring up-and-coming
actors of the 1990s (including the likes of Alicia Silverstone and Shannen Doherty) and directed by established directors such as William Friedkin, Joe Dante, and Ralph Bakshi.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Rodriguez was the only young director to participate in the series.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
The series was produced by the son and daughter of Samuel Z.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Arkoff, the co-founder and producer of American International Pictures (AIP),
the distributor of the films this series takes its titles from.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Robert Rodriguez's take concerned a rebel named Dude Delaney (David Arquette) who dreams of leaving his dead end small town and becoming a
rockabilly star but gets caught up in a nasty feud with the town's local sheriff (William Sadler) and his son (Jason Wiles).

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Salma Hayek plays Dude's girlfriend, Donna.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film explores themes of car race, texas,
juvenile delinquent, 1950s, young girl.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
